author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A prerequisite recorded as blocks on the blocker produces the same readiness classification as the mirrored blocked_by row, proved by a paired test over both spellings; The disposition of the 219 existing blocks rows is recorded and applied, either by canonicalizing them on write or by resolving the reverse direction at read time; The blocker set pm next reports for the five currently affected items names the blocks gate, and pm-p1g43q is no longer classified ready while pm-07pt16 is open; The downstream unblocks projection resolves the same reverse direction as blocker resolution, with a test that fails if only one of the two is fixed; A check fails when an ordering kind accepted by the write path is not reachable by blocker resolution, so a new spelling cannot reintroduce the divergence"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: high
confidence: 95
resolution: Corpus-aware reverse blocks resolution shared across readiness and auto-unblock
expected_result: "blocks and blocked_by produce identical readiness, blocker, unblocks, and close-time behavior"
actual_result: Reverse blocks targets are classified blocked; downstream unblocks and close candidates share the resolver; registry conformance test prevents future ordering-kind drift; live pm-p1g43q evidence passes
